                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                        "entry_id": "22f0519d-fa30-30db-b684-d4c8dbbb3e4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A student of Cambridge University."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0019e902-a710-4e7f-b6d0-89f271f85cee",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "You should have been there---it was a good race. Just to clarify matters for the hard of understanding, the tabs led for about 1500m before turning to shrapnel, and Oxford eventually won by 3/4 length."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65b1c71e-2bb5-4357-8a5a-c4fb08e71b56",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "Before Rachel gets in with a stab at the Tabs' coxing efforts, may I say that my experience of coxes on the Isis is somewhat similar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7d92a43-dca3-4764-8928-e88179dd43d4",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "Plus, there's always been a healthy rivalry between the tabs and us, but I'm sure this has nothing to do with it ;-)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f9db23e-e0bb-4e8b-b56f-6722d4f59b9e",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "I hope the Tabs get beaten! :-) I support Oxford for no real reason but they have a bad habit of losing to Cambridge recently."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1aa13e04-a6f0-4d62-94ec-c66be17dc0fe",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "I have nothing against the girl (other than the fact she's a tab!), but it does strike me as a little daft!!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97ff0a75-194d-4872-8f27-15258d2cd3e1",
                                                "sense_id": "1180a228-cfd5-370d-8a5f-52f5cf8430af",
                                                "text": "Anybody know who won? ¶ Or should that be, how much did the Tabs win by? ;-)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tab",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "703d2bef-c645-389a-8316-34d6d3f89869",
                                        "entry_id": "baa3feff-20ac-33bb-9582-0387c7a1a4d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tabloid newspaper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e1531f7-d941-4dcb-9e55-2df09cbe1da7",
                                                "sense_id": "703d2bef-c645-389a-8316-34d6d3f89869",
                                                "text": "By 1926 the tabloid mania was at full tilt, and the tabs in New York went at each other with hammer and tong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "327562d7-ca07-4291-a944-8804b4c8d9db",
                                                "sense_id": "703d2bef-c645-389a-8316-34d6d3f89869",
                                                "text": "The tabloids were able to spend much of the week confronting their demons. Maxine Carr's request to be released from prison early prompted the tabs to let her know what they thought of her suggestion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e0c31b4-720a-4f25-8751-e350806e54ca",
                                                "sense_id": "703d2bef-c645-389a-8316-34d6d3f89869",
                                                "text": "That is the attitude of the tabs: they cover the world's most important city."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e124a4c-6a16-44d5-a79d-f0b5e1c821c2",
                                                "sense_id": "703d2bef-c645-389a-8316-34d6d3f89869",
                                                "text": "If ministers disappoint—they usually do—the tabloids can cry \"betrayal\". They never lose. But just because the tabs are often flagrantly dishonest (in more expensive papers you get a better class of dishonesty) doesn't mean they're always wrong."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tab",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f70132a0-483e-345f-a252-90f0f6011d03",
                                        "entry_id": "57ff80e1-75e3-30cb-a904-35e7a08c1ff8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tablet, especially one containing illicit drugs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32594eda-53e3-43f6-bdc8-ee1f9de11fab",
                                                "sense_id": "f70132a0-483e-345f-a252-90f0f6011d03",
                                                "text": "Tonight the kids will go out and party down in a more righteous mode. Alcohol and not a few tabs of X will be ingested. Club music will throb through big speakers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
